:"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T04:13:31-07:00","id":1074085,"title":"","content":"The thread has been quiet for a while, so I just wanted to say hi to all my fellow Geist-watchers (much like nessie, whale and bird watcher we are constantly looking for sightings of our selected creatures) and see if anyone had heard anything new. The Mondays Meeting Blog this week showed Geist 2E as the second book listed under Second Draft (all but 1 of the books that have been in that slot before Geist having moved up the ranks) so I eagerly hope and await for the Blog that will show Geist 2E in the Development stage (at which point I dearly hope we may see some dev blogs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). Hope this finds everyone on the forums and in Onyx Path in good spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T11:07:04-07:00","id":1074238,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling Geist is going to follow Promethean's model of open dev blog - few and far between. I hope I'm wrong, but that's the impression I'm getting, considering how little we know with it already in second draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T11:42:18-07:00","id":1074252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1074238#post1074238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a feeling Geist is going to follow Promethean's model of open dev blog - few and far between. I hope I'm wrong, but that's the impression I'm getting, considering how little we know with it already in second draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could form another Underworld River from our tears, if that is true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:00:55-07:00","id":1075887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1074238#post1074238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a feeling Geist is going to follow Promethean's model of open dev blog - few and far between. I hope I'm wrong, but that's the impression I'm getting, considering how little we know with it already in second draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dead Dominions are well-guarded and hidden far beyond mortal perception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T09:15:33-07:00","id":1076533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1074252#post1074252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could form another Underworld River from our tears, if that is true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there an existing River of Tears? (I can't recall off the top of my head, and I'm away form my books). If not, there should be, so if they can make that happen ... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:21:02-07:00","id":1077470,"title":"","content":"Why are they called Sin-Eaters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:26:24-07:00","id":1077472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1077470#post1077470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are they called Sin-Eaters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-Eaters are a type of medium in various cultures who supernaturally aids the cleansing of dead people so they can move into the afterlife. So bound who help ghosts move on use that term to describe themselves since it's pretty accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T21:09:51-07:00","id":1077497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1077472#post1077472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sin-Eaters are a type of medium in various cultures who supernaturally aids the cleansing of dead people so they can move into the afterlife. So bound who help ghosts move on use that term to describe themselves since it's pretty accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do the Archetypes fit into this? Ones like Advocate are obvious, but what about guys like Bonepickers and Celebrants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T21:16:29-07:00","id":1077501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1077497#post1077497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But do the Archetypes fit into this? Ones like Advocate are obvious, but what about guys like Bonepickers and Celebrants?</div> </div> </div> </div>Archetypes don't fit into it, whether an individual bound is a sin-eater is entirely separate from their archetype. A bonepicker who is a sin-eater might do things like buy houses that are haunted and have low-prices, clear out the ghosts and sell it at a much higher price. A celebrant could be a sin-eater because it's entertaining and thrilling to be fighting ghosts and solving murders.<br /> <br /> But that might not apply in 2e, since archetypes might be handled differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-13-2017, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T21:23:47-07:00","id":1077505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1077501#post1077501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archetypes don't fit into it, whether an individual bound is a sin-eater is entirely separate from their archetype. A bonepicker who is a sin-eater might do things like buy houses that are haunted and have low-prices, clear out the ghosts and sell it at a much higher price. A celebrant could be a sin-eater because it's entertaining and thrilling to be fighting ghosts and solving murders.<br /> <br /> But that might not apply in 2e, since archetypes might be handled differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Archetypes sound more like, well, <i>archetype </i>anchor traits like vampiric Dirge &amp; Mask and changeling Mask &amp; Mien, rather than philosophies like Refinements or Agendas. I assume the original intent was to have Bound Archetypes be equivalents of the latter, but right now they lack the same 'weight.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T21:57:02-07:00","id":1077517,"title":"","content":"I might have imagined it but I thought the dev said there is more than one group of Bound and the Sin Eaters are the name for the more Advocate type. I don't remember names given for other Bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T22:05:11-07:00","id":1077524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1077517#post1077517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have imagined it but I thought the dev said there is more than one group of Bound and the Sin Eaters are the name for the more Advocate type. I don't remember names given for other Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>iirc he said there are more than one group of bound, and that the Sin-Eaters are simply the type of Bound that players are assumed to be in the same way Forsaken are assumed to be the type of Uratha that are being played. Which was already true in 1e, but maybe they're making it more obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:39:55-07:00","id":1077557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1077505#post1077505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Archetypes sound more like, well, <i>archetype </i>anchor traits like vampiric Dirge &amp; Mask and changeling Mask &amp; Mien, rather than philosophies like Refinements or Agendas. I assume the original intent was to have Bound Archetypes be equivalents of the latter, but right now they lack the same 'weight.'</div> </div> </div> </div>They seem pretty agenda-y to me, and each is a philosophy of &quot;What am I going to do now&quot; rather than a personality aspect. So I'm not sure I really understand the issue from that point of view (I do have issues with Archetypes, it's just what I've described doesn't seem to be one of them to me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:42:50-07:00","id":1077558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1077557#post1077557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They seem pretty agenda-y to me, and each is a philosophy of &quot;What am I going to do now&quot; rather than a personality aspect. So I'm not sure I really understand the issue from that point of view (I do have issues with Archetypes, it's just what I've described doesn't seem to be one of them to me).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, it does seem to be so when put it that way. I guess we won't know for sure until it comes out. Meanwhile I'm hoping that Archetypes get more shine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:07:56-07:00","id":1077955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1077524#post1077524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">iirc he said there are more than one group of bound, and that the Sin-Eaters are simply the type of Bound that players are assumed to be in the same way Forsaken are assumed to be the type of Uratha that are being played. Which was already true in 1e, but maybe they're making it more obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I walked away under the impression that the Sin Eater group of Bound were the players and had a broad shared philosophy like the Forsaken. The Sin Eaters would tend to believe in acting as intermediaries between mortal and ghost worlds. An archetype would be more of an approach to life than an agenda. This would all be made more obvious than in the 1e. Details might change but it would be more clear why the players are called Sin Eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:40:14-07:00","id":1078633,"title":"","content":"That may meam not all the old archetypes are going to make it to being new ones. Like if Sineaters are the Bound who act as intermediaries, then the Sineater Y-splats might include Advocates (who do ghosts' business), Gatekeepers (who stop the two worlds messing with each other), and Pilgrims (who teach the living not to end up as ghosts) - while Reapers (who kill people they think need killing) or Bonepickers (who just look out for themselves) might be other factions of Bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:50:28-07:00","id":1078671,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I've mentioned this before; but I'm hoping that 2e completely overhauls Archetypes, revising what they represent in a manner similar to how C2e's Seemings got reimagined from \u201cbroad classes of Kiths\u201d to \u201chow you reclaimed agency\u201d. I don't have a clear notion of what 2e Archetypes should be; but \u201chow you reacted to your near-death experience\u201d just doesn't feel right to me. Maybe something more along the lines of \u201cwhat kind of geist did you join with?\u201d, and possibly associating them with Haunts(?: what used to be Manifestations before ghosts co-opted the name), much like Keys are associated with Thresholds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:51:42-07:00","id":1078672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1078633#post1078633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That may meam not all the old archetypes are going to make it to being new ones. Like if Sineaters are the Bound who act as intermediaries, then the Sineater Y-splats might include Advocates (who do ghosts' business), Gatekeepers (who stop the two worlds messing with each other), and Pilgrims (who teach the living not to end up as ghosts) - while Reapers (who kill people they think need killing) or Bonepickers (who just look out for themselves) might be other factions of Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really understand why that would be the case when &quot;Sineaters are the Bound who get rid of ghosts&quot; was true in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T18:01:10-07:00","id":1078676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1078672#post1078672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really understand why that would be the case when &quot;Sineaters are the Bound who get rid of ghosts&quot; was true in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some archetypes have that as a focus, while for others it's more peripheral: Celebrants may try to go their whole lives without seeing any ghosts, while Mourners pretty much think they're still dead, and Reapers mostly get rid of living people. So perhaps the Archetypes will be changed round to make the part about dealing with ghosts being more explicitly what distinguishes Sineaters from other Bound - or perhaps not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T20:21:47-07:00","id":1078730,"title":"","content":"Maybe something like this for Archetypes and how they do sin-eating?<br /> Advocates; resolve ghosts' Anchors<br /> Bonepickers; perform something for ghosts and get paid<br /> Celebrants; provide joys of the living world to ghosts<br /> Gatekeepers; maintain Avernian Gates so that troublemakers on either side don't pass by<br /> Mourners; help the ghost accept that it's dead, and it's time to move on<br /> Necromancers; dive into the Underworld directly<br /> Pilgrims; mark and study sites of mass death, or particularly important deaths<br /> Reapers; kill both living people who mess with ghosts, and ghosts who mess with living people<br /> <br /> EDIT: On second thought, what I wrote for Mourners and Pilgrims should be reversed. Also, expected affinity Haunts if we're getting them:<br /> Advocate - Curse<br /> Bonepicker - Marionette<br /> Celebrant - Shroud<br /> Gatekeeper - Boneyard<br /> Mourner - Caul<br /> Necromancer - Pit<br /> Pilgrim - Oracle<br /> Reaper - Rage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-14-2017, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T09:49:04-07:00","id":1078934,"title":"","content":"While working on a gmc patch to use Geist in my 2e mage game, I treated the archetypes exactly like Demon Agendas. They're pretty similar, so it worked well: personal philosophies that gives bonuses to the way they approach a problem.<br /> The player who wanted to be a sin eater chose Necromancer, so thats the only archetype condition I wrote... <br /> I'm very excited to see what the developers do with archetypes, but this was a an effective patch","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T11:51:17-07:00","id":1078988,"title":"","content":"Dave said on 4chan that he is expanding the rules for ghosts to be playable characters and that Geist is almost in development (or at least further than Changeling is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T11:55:56-07:00","id":1078989,"title":"","content":"Further than Changeling? But Changeling has spent quite some time in development while Geist is still in second draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T12:10:43-07:00","id":1078997,"title":"","content":"so looking towards this game. Definetly gonna back the kickstarter<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T13:27:50-07:00","id":1079024,"title":"","content":"If there is one. That's far from certain unless I've missed some news.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T22:30:53-07:00","id":1080189,"title":"","content":"The core problem of the 1st-edition Geist (for me) was a wide gap between what game was intended for and what tools it gave to roleplay it. These didn't match at all.<br /> So, what tools the 2nd edition will provide to reflect the GAME OF SECOND CHANCES into the game-mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T04:36:39-07:00","id":1080244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1080189#post1080189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core problem of the 1st-edition Geist (for me) was a wide gap between what game was intended for and what tools it gave to roleplay it. These didn't match at all.<br /> So, what tools the 2nd edition will provide to reflect the GAME OF SECOND CHANCES into the game-mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div> What type of mechanics was it missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T05:03:00-07:00","id":1080247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1080244#post1080244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What type of mechanics was it missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't find any represenation of Second Chances (the sub-title of the game) in the powers, moraltrait or ways to restore WP or gain experience.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf the Sawage Fury was in Kuruth and Primal Urge (2nd edition added Hunt as a central part of mechanics!)<br /> In Vampire the Modern Gothic was in the Humanity and Beast (Gothic Morals at it's hubris).<br /> In Mage Gnosis and Wisdom were the keys to Modern Sorcery (The balance between knowledge and wisdom as a central part of the very theme of magic)<br /> In Changeling, the Clarity ang Glamour are the very essence to Beautiful Madness.<br /> In Promethean the stolen lives are in the Wasteland and Disquiet (their own lives don't belong to them, stolen from the world).<br /> <br /> And what about Geist? Where are the Second Chances in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 04-18-2017, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:06:09-07:00","id":1080278,"title":"","content":"Right here /snare drums<br /> <br /> ... I'll let myself out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:12:11-07:00","id":1080281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1080247#post1080247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't find any represenation of Second Chances (the sub-title of the game) in the powers, moraltrait or ways to restore WP or gain experience.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf the Sawage Fury was in Kuruth and Primal Urge (2nd edition added Hunt as a central part of mechanics!)<br /> In Vampire the Modern Gothic was in the Humanity and Beast (Gothic Morals at it's hubris).<br /> In Mage Gnosis and Wisdom were the keys to Modern Sorcery (The balance between knowledge and wisdom as a central part of the very theme of magic)<br /> In Changeling, the Clarity ang Glamour are the very essence to Beautiful Madness.<br /> In Promethean the stolen lives are in the Wasteland and Disquiet (their own lives don't belong to them, stolen from the world).<br /> <br /> And what about Geist? Where are the Second Chances in it?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the fact that they've come back from the dead? They can do that multiple times. They also give ghosts a second chance to take care of whatever is keeping them there in the world of the living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:26:47-07:00","id":1080337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about the fact that they've come back from the dead? </div> </div> </div>Vampires too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can do that multiple times. </div> </div> </div>Prometheans too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They also give ghosts a second chance to take care of whatever is keeping them there in the world of the living. </div> </div> </div>How is it reflected in game-mechanics? What tools does the crunch part of the system offers for it? And how does crunch motivate <i>players </i>to do it? What <i>thematic </i>reward offers system for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 04-18-2017, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:40:15-07:00","id":1080346,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6186\" data-vbnamecard=\"6186\">Aleksay</a>, I'm with you - I also did not seen very much 'Second Chances' in mechanics or in-setting solutions. ( Beside character returning to life once with Geist the first time. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:56:54-07:00","id":1080356,"title":"","content":"My hope for 2e is that Synergy can be made to re-enforce this concept. Second Chances for the Bound, second chances for the Geist, second chances for Ghosts, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:12:37-07:00","id":1080367,"title":"","content":"Alkesay and Wyrdhamster, I disagree with you both completely. What kind of mechanic are you looking for to provide 'second chances'? Also, in terms of in-setting solutions...that's what they storyteller is supposed to help illustrate... I've run numerous games and in each one, the character were compelled to help the ghosts, not by me telling them to, but because of the way they built their characters, read the rules and setting, and so on. <br /> <br /> I don't understand what kind of mechanic would be wanted to 'provide a second chance'. This makes no sense to me. A Game of second changes...the tag line is about the second chance the characters have at life after their death. If you look at the type of characters that can be built, they all represent how their lives will be with their second chances...some use this to help others pass on, some use this to celebrate all that life has to offer, some use this to enact a type of justice to those that would harm lives, etc. etc. I mean, that says it right there does it not? Not to mention the fact that these powers that the characters are granted are used to actually enact these things. Not just for 'fun'. Of course, you could just play randomly and without any type of motive behind your character's actions,etc. but would you even enjoy that? I mean what would be the end-game then?<br /> <br /> Of course, as someone who has had this since its inception, maybe I'm a little jaded, but even after the first time reading it, I understood how it would work towards that straight away...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:56:28-07:00","id":1080393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EldritchMinister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1080367#post1080367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand what kind of mechanic would be wanted to 'provide a second chance'. This makes no sense to me. A Game of second changes...the tag line is about the second chance the characters have at life after their death. If you look at the type of characters that can be built, they all represent how their lives will be with their second chances...some use this to help others pass on, some use this to celebrate all that life has to offer, some use this to enact a type of justice to those that would harm lives, etc. etc. I mean, that says it right there does it not? Not to mention the fact that these powers that the characters are granted are used to actually enact these things. Not just for 'fun'. Of course, you could just play randomly and without any type of motive behind your character's actions,etc. but would you even enjoy that? I mean what would be the end-game then?</div> </div> </div> </div>If all that is about Second Chances is that characters become Bound by death and coming once again to life, it's like saying that <b>Vampire</b> is game about everlasting hunger as you only <i>once</i> feed on your Sire on Embrace and later non at all. Or that <b>Mage</b> is game about sorcerers because you cast <i>one </i>spell at Awakening - and later you cannot. Or that <b>Promethean</b> is game about stolen lives and alchemy just because they are once Created and later do not learn any Alchemy. Or <b>Beast</b> being game about Hunger and you do not need to feed your Horror every session a bit.<br /> <br /> We all know it's simply not true and all games support their basic premise by <b><i>all the life</i></b> of their PCs. Mages cast spells and uncover Mysteries all the time. Prometheans are living and breathing Alchemy, always changing. Vampires are all the time hunger for blood and power. Werewolves need at least once in 3 months ( on low Primal Urge ) to Hunt, or they become true monsters.<br /> <br /> So how Second Chances can return as motif in mechanics of <b>Geist</b> game? Maybe Sin Eaters can 'stole' part's of resolved ghosts histories? They can resolve tragedy and made themselves forever part of story? Something like Demons stealing 'lives' of their Covers? ( Like getting Skills or Merits from this? ) Or maybe Sin-Eaters let ghosts once again <i>LIVE</i>, like granting their new bodies? Or that Bounds help living mortals also, to rise from their lives 'dead end'? You know, Second Chances beside 'I returned from grave once, now what to do with my life'. Giving someone real SECOND CHANCE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T10:12:55-07:00","id":1080404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, you could just play randomly and without any type of motive behind your character's actions,etc. </div> </div> </div>And nothing would affect it. You can act as ravenous maniac in Vampire, and Beast would devour you. It's the core of gothic.<br /> You can try to hide from your nature and duty in Werewolf, but your nature will find you. It's the core of savage.<br /> And if you just want to celebrate the whole new life in Geist, saying &quot;f*ck it! I'm a ghost-powered superhero!&quot;, how will the core theme reflect this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T10:37:24-07:00","id":1080418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1080393#post1080393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all that is about Second Chances is that characters become Bound by death and coming once again to life, it's like saying that <b>Vampire</b> is game about everlasting hunger as you only <i>once</i> feed on your Sire on Embrace and later non at all. Or that <b>Mage</b> is game about sorcerers because you cast <i>one </i>spell at Awakening - and later you cannot. Or that <b>Promethean</b> is game about stolen lives and alchemy just because they are once Created and later do not learn any Alchemy. Or <b>Beast</b> being game about Hunger and you do not need to feed your Horror every session a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are all false analogues. When you feed you stop being hungry. When you're done casting a spell you're no longer actively practicing magic. But when you're resurrected by your Geist you <i>don't stop having your second chance</i>. Every single session will relate to their second chance because <i>everything your character's doing is part of their second chance</i>.<br /> Of course there needs to be more than just that in order to properly reinforce the theme (which I too would like to learn more about), but you're severely underselling the importance of the Bargain. It <i>is </i>something that does affect them through <i>all their lives</i>. It's just easier to ignore. Both because of the lack of known mechanics that support that theme, and because it's a very broad/vague theme in comparison to the other gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T10:44:22-07:00","id":1080423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1080418#post1080418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are all false analogues. When you feed you stop being hungry. When you're done casting a spell you're no longer actively practicing magic. But when you're resurrected by your Geist you <i>don't stop having your second chance</i>. Every single session will relate to their second chance because <i>everything your character's doing is part of their second chance</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you never stop <i>giving</i> that second chance, because the geist is getting one too. And you never stop being able to give it to others, because every problem that a ghost died to soon to fix is something <i>you</i> can fix - and yes, there are other games where you might be able to do that for a ghost, but none where it's what the game is <i>about</i>. And Sineaters in first edition benefit hard by granting that second chance (fixing the ghost's issues) or taking it away forever (eating the ghost).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:31:34-07:00","id":1080450,"title":"","content":"I guess this is where we differ. I mean we can go back and forth on what you think reinforces the game versus what I believe reinforces the game. But that can be said with all of these game lines. I have had some very successful Geist games that I have been part of both player and some long running Chronicles that I have been storyteller. They have all been very character driven and in each one, despite different gaming groups altogether, the players have all exhibited some sort of lending aid to the ghosts that have not passed on and protected the living from dead that would do them wrong, etc. I have yet to run or be part of a game that those playing felt that the premise of Geist was lost. These stories varied quite a bit, but all focused on the fact that these characters had a second chance at life and they were not wasting it (not in terms of, I'm going to just use my &quot;super powers&quot; for fucking around either).<br /> <br /> At any rate, I am looking forward to 2E. This game line is probably my favorite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":12143,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","user":"EldritchMinister","date":". 04-18-2017, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T13:50:15-07:00","id":1080537,"title":"","content":"Totally agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12143_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12143\" data-vbnamecard=\"12143\">EldritchMinister</a> here. I don't even see how that concept could be strange or incomprehensible, honestly.<br /> Additionally, I don't think the thematic core needs to be directly represented by mechanics like Synergy or something similar, but it sounds like some of you guys want that (which is fine for your game tables, I simply see it differently).<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6186\" data-vbnamecard=\"6186\">Aleksay</a> re:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> saying &quot;f*ck it! I'm a ghost-powered superhero!&quot;, how will the core theme reflect this? </div> </div> </div>First of all, going I AM A SUPERHERO is a completely valid decision about what to do with your newfound live and powers - you could say, what to do with your <b>second chance </b>at life.<br /> And since you seemed to be mostly interested in what consequences there are with ignoring the 'calling', so to speak: Ghosts notice Bound, and are drawn to them. There WILL be consequences when you try to ignore them, because being constantly swarmed by an ever-increasing number of Ghosts trying to make you do something for them simply is not an opportunity an ST would let go to create Drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T14:27:15-07:00","id":1080556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1080537#post1080537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12143_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12143\" data-vbnamecard=\"12143\">EldritchMinister</a> here. I don't even see how that concept could be strange or incomprehensible, honestly.<br /> Additionally, I don't think the thematic core needs to be directly represented by mechanics like Synergy or something similar, but it sounds like some of you guys want that (which is fine for your game tables, I simply see it differently).<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6186\" data-vbnamecard=\"6186\">Aleksay</a> re:<br /> <br /> First of all, going I AM A SUPERHERO is a completely valid decision about what to do with your newfound live and powers - you could say, what to do with your <b>second chance </b>at life.<br /> And since you seemed to be mostly interested in what consequences there are with ignoring the 'calling', so to speak: Ghosts notice Bound, and are drawn to them. There WILL be consequences when you try to ignore them, because being constantly swarmed by an ever-increasing number of Ghosts trying to make you do something for them simply is not an opportunity an ST would let go to create Drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also? Superheroes would tend to create a fair amount of Ghosts as a byproduct of their activities, I'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T16:22:07-07:00","id":1080619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1080537#post1080537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, going I AM A SUPERHERO is a completely valid decision about what to do with your newfound live and powers - you could say, what to do with your <b>second chance </b>at life.<br /> And since you seemed to be mostly interested in what consequences there are with ignoring the 'calling', so to speak: Ghosts notice Bound, and are drawn to them. There WILL be consequences when you try to ignore them, because being constantly swarmed by an ever-increasing number of Ghosts trying to make you do something for them simply is not an opportunity an ST would let go to create Drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, in fact, the character concept that got me excited enough about Geist to try running it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T16:39:19-07:00","id":1080632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1080393#post1080393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If all that is about Second Chances is that characters become Bound by death and coming once again to life, it's like saying that <b>Vampire</b> is game about everlasting hunger as you only <i>once</i> feed on your Sire on Embrace and later non at all. Or that <b>Mage</b> is game about sorcerers because you cast <i>one </i>spell at Awakening - and later you cannot. Or that <b>Promethean</b> is game about stolen lives and alchemy just because they are once Created and later do not learn any Alchemy. Or <b>Beast</b> being game about Hunger and you do not need to feed your Horror every session a bit.<br /> <br /> We all know it's simply not true and all games support their basic premise by <b><i>all the life</i></b> of their PCs. Mages cast spells and uncover Mysteries all the time. Prometheans are living and breathing Alchemy, always changing. Vampires are all the time hunger for blood and power. Werewolves need at least once in 3 months ( on low Primal Urge ) to Hunt, or they become true monsters.<br /> <br /> So how Second Chances can return as motif in mechanics of <b>Geist</b> game? Maybe Sin Eaters can 'stole' part's of resolved ghosts histories? They can resolve tragedy and made themselves forever part of story? Something like Demons stealing 'lives' of their Covers? ( Like getting Skills or Merits from this? ) Or maybe Sin-Eaters let ghosts once again <i>LIVE</i>, like granting their new bodies? Or that Bounds help living mortals also, to rise from their lives 'dead end'? You know, Second Chances beside 'I returned from grave once, now what to do with my life'. Giving someone real SECOND CHANCE.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why of that is needed. But: what if every time you resolve a ghost's unfinished business, you in effect earn some \u201ccredit\u201d in the \u201cLife Exchange\u201d? When a Sin-Eater comes back to life, there are consequences (such as a fraying of Synergy and someone else dying). What if helping or destroying a ghosts earned some sort of special experience that can be spent to mitigate or prevent such consequences? Is that the short of thing you're thinking of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T23:22:10-07:00","id":1080757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1080632#post1080632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why of that is needed. But: what if every time you resolve a ghost's unfinished business, you in effect earn some \u201ccredit\u201d in the \u201cLife Exchange\u201d? When a Sin-Eater comes back to life, there are consequences (such as a fraying of Synergy and someone else dying). What if helping or destroying a ghosts earned some sort of special experience that can be spent to mitigate or prevent such consequences? Is that the short of thing you're thinking of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like Fate Points in <b>Warhammer</b>? Hmm, this could be interesting. Collecting ghosts to have MORE 'second chances' to spend in your new life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T17:08:52-07:00","id":1081179,"title":"","content":"Or, expanding on the thought, the currency might also be used to grant \u201csecond chances\u201d to others, perhaps through your krewe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T05:22:44-07:00","id":1081394,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'm following this at all. Please elaborate, if you will. What do you mean 'more second chances to spend'? The whole idea behind second chances is the second chance YOUR character has gained by merging (for lack of a better term of course) with the Geist and what you do afterwards with the gifts bestowed upon your second chance. You now have the ability to see those that have not passed on and enter Twilight to engage more with them...you have manifestations that can help you achieve these things. You are wanting some sort of game mechanic that forces the player characters to do good for others in the game? Is that what this is coming down to? This way it would be an integral part instead of leaving it to the players and ST to point this out in story? <br /> <br /> Like what has been mentioned, you can ignore the ghosts that see you and come to you (they all now know you...or can get to know you...) for aid, but think of how that would drive one insane. You would almost (at least a character I would play) get to a point that you would appease them and help them for your own sanity and mental rest. One of the things that I enjoy about Geist is the fact that it does not force you into a certain role, but allows you the space to choose your role and also allows the ST the space to create a story that NEEDS your characters to help the others. Some would say that this was TOO broad and should have been a bit more narrow. I can see that too, but again, I'm partial to Geist is one of my favorite games even in it's 1.1 edition. You also have to think of the Geist...there are wants and needs for the Geist that need to be fulfilled. You don't want to risk having a takeover....there was an SAS that the character was completely taken over by the Geist...Ah! Dem Bones. It was a nice take on the idea of what happens when you are overpowered by your Geist and lose control.<br /> <br /> The idea of currency used to grant 'second chances' to others, you mean allowing a Geist to merge during death? Or perhaps seeing their death and stopping it altogether? I mean I think that could work, however, there would have to be some serious consequences to something like that as you are now taking away from the cycle of life and death...hmmm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T18:24:46-07:00","id":1081651,"title":"","content":"Not to cut in but my hope for 2e is that it will cover more of how sin eater's interact with ghost stories. not just ghosts but the actual stories surrounding them and how you can interact and resolve them. every ghost is a tragic ending but they don't have to stay that way. The 2e line has been really great about getting you into the headspace and experience of being whatever your template is (how vampires interact with their beasts and sense blood, mages' obsessions and mage sight, ect.) and i'm really looking forward to getting into the headspace of a sin eater.<br /> I'm also hoping for a major overhaul of the manifestations when they become haunts. Alot of the powers in 1e were very much combat based so it seemed to encourage fighting and those abilities that wern't were almost overpowered when dealing with ghosts so it might clear up any real intrigue or mystery to fast which isn't really great in a game about ghost stories. I prefered alot of the ceremonies and would like to see more abilities fall into their more subtle line. I'd like to see the powers as a little more spooky and a little less dangerous.<br /> And i'd really like to see more about the mystery cult aspect of krews and the dead conspiracies. Cults have kinda been a major thing in chronicles of darkness since god machine came out and i'd like to see that apply here. Death, ghost and funerary cults are a really cool thing in games and i'd like to see some stuff on that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 04-21-2017, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T03:46:00-07:00","id":1102478,"title":"","content":"Hi all! It's been a few months since anyone has posted, so I thought I'd ask, any new tidbits about Geist 2nd Edition out there? The Monday Meeting Notes place it squarely in the Second Draft stage, one stage behind the Changeling 2nd Edition, so fingers crossed for a move into the Development stage and some Open Dev previews <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T07:51:56-07:00","id":1102506,"title":"","content":"Last bit of information was got was from DaveB, who teased he is working revamped fully playable ghosts for the book, and did say the book was pretty much practically at development stage. Though that being said, I'm not sure if the playable ghosts are taking over the minor template that Filamena Young was mentioned to work on earlier for the book. Would be pretty neat if the book does end up including playable rules for a Sin-Eater, Ghost and Minor Template, but I can totally understand if that takes up a good chunk of wordcount and is relegated to another book down the line.<br /> <br /> Think it was also mentioned that Geist 2e will likely be the next corebook to come out, with Changeling having a slight delay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T10:42:20-07:00","id":1102559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1102506#post1102506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last bit of information was got was from DaveB, who teased he is working revamped fully playable ghosts for the book, and did say the book was pretty much practically at development stage. Though that being said, I'm not sure if the playable ghosts are taking over the minor template that Filamena Young was mentioned to work on earlier for the book. Would be pretty neat if the book does end up including playable rules for a Sin-Eater, Ghost and Minor Template, but I can totally understand if that takes up a good chunk of wordcount and is relegated to another book down the line.<br /> <br /> Think it was also mentioned that Geist 2e will likely be the next corebook to come out, with Changeling having a slight delay.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be surprised if Geist made it out before Hunter, but you never know. While Geist nominally looks to be ahead, different stages work at different paces for different leads. That said, I have loved Geist for a long time, so I certainly wouldn't mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T12:42:41-07:00","id":1102582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1102506#post1102506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last bit of information was got was from DaveB, who teased he is working revamped fully playable ghosts for the book, and did say the book was pretty much practically at development stage. Though that being said, I'm not sure if the playable ghosts are taking over the minor template that Filamena Young was mentioned to work on earlier for the book. Would be pretty neat if the book does end up including playable rules for a Sin-Eater, Ghost and Minor Template, but I can totally understand if that takes up a good chunk of wordcount and is relegated to another book down the line.<br /> <br /> Think it was also mentioned that Geist 2e will likely be the next corebook to come out, with Changeling having a slight delay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'll add that in. I loved Filamena's minor templates in VtR2, WtF2 &amp; MtAw2. Really hope we finally see a minor template for Geist. And given that Mage the Awakening 2E had both the Sleepwalker and the Proximi, maybe they'll be two entries in the supporting cast appendix. Which forum post did Dave make mention of the playable ghost? I want to be sure to follow it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","user":"Robert D","date":". 06-11-2017, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T13:07:55-07:00","id":1102591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1102559#post1102559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be surprised if Geist made it out before Hunter, but you never know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Geist was put in second drafts in February and Hunter entered first drafts in January. Future hold-ups aside, what else convinces you Hunter will be out sooner?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T13:13:36-07:00","id":1102594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1102591#post1102591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Geist was put in second drafts in February and Hunter entered first drafts in January. Future hold-ups aside, what else convinces you Hunter will be out sooner?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just that Hunter started sooner and that Rich meantioned when Geist went into first drafts that different Devs take different lengths of time to complete different stages, so each project is very individual in its development process. He specifically meantioned that some lead devs will go quickly in early stages then slow in the later stages, while others operate the other way around. It all depends on individual style. <br /> <br /> That said, I fully acknowledge that I could be completely wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T15:35:22-07:00","id":1102628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1102506#post1102506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last bit of information was got was from DaveB, who teased he is working revamped fully playable ghosts for the book, and did say the book was pretty much practically at development stage. Though that being said, I'm not sure if the playable ghosts are taking over the minor template that Filamena Young was mentioned to work on earlier for the book. Would be pretty neat if the book does end up including playable rules for a Sin-Eater, Ghost and Minor Template, but I can totally understand if that takes up a good chunk of wordcount and is relegated to another book down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh awesome, regarding playable ghosts. My ultimate fantasy version of Geist would have a sort of W-axis as to whether you're playing Bound, revenants, ghosts, or even mediums - but I acknowledge that's quite some overkill. But some of the others are coming in as minor templates, that would be great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1102591#post1102591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Geist was put in second drafts in February and Hunter entered first drafts in January. Future hold-ups aside, what else convinces you Hunter will be out sooner?</div> </div> </div> </div>Monica's also juggling a <i>lot</i> for Hunter - and considering it has to take the other game into account enough to be able to kinda duplicate them, I could see her being a little glad of the idea of Geist overtaking it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T14:40:15-07:00","id":1108147,"title":"","content":"According to today's meeting notes, Geist 2E is officially in the Development stage!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T15:04:05-07:00","id":1108160,"title":"","content":"Forgot about it before but after coming to note the progress of Geist, I thought I should point out that Hunter had to begin from scratch and Geist was obviously being considered and unofficially worked on long before it made it on the schedule which is why it went through the first stage so fast. Assuming equal pacing, Geist should actually come out before Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T15:22:14-07:00","id":1108166,"title":"","content":"That's not without precedent. C20 is out; Wr20 isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T19:37:17-07:00","id":1108232,"title":"","content":"Hopefully the next thing we find out about the book is it's full title/subtitle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:51:32-07:00","id":1108269,"title":"","content":"If anything, I just hope we get to know just what those &quot;masked ghosts&quot; are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T04:21:14-07:00","id":1108343,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping they'll tell us about what 2e Thresholds and Archetypes (hope that name &quot;archetype&quot; changed) are like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T04:57:47-07:00","id":1108354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1108269#post1108269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, I just hope we get to know just what those &quot;masked ghosts&quot; are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the new Antagonists and the new reworked system to make Geists more mechanically relevant have me the most interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T05:49:20-07:00","id":1108359,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure one of the new antagonist types is a variety of Bound who have taken on cthonians rather than geister","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T01:33:43-07:00","id":1108661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1108359#post1108359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure one of the new antagonist types is a variety of Bound who have taken on cthonians rather than geister</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not mistaken, while the concept of such antagonist was mentioned a number of times, it was always said to be more of a &quot;Night Horrors&quot; material than a core book antagonist","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T14:15:37-07:00","id":1108931,"title":"","content":"I think they were mentioned as being the original Bound in Dark Eras, back when the Underworld was entirely flooded with the Ocean of Fragments. If I recall I think it was mentioned to be a topic for a possible supplement book alongside Bound who have multiple geists attached to them. Though that could also mean as either antagonist or playable, which would be neat. Beetlejuice/Blood Mary types of ghost entities (Urban legend ghosts that are summoned by uttering their name or otherwise) were also mentioned to be a neat idea for a supplement book.<br /> <br /> Though for the corebook for what has already been revealed so far, there are no abmortals or standard ghosts under the antagonist section of the book, though it will be half/half new and old antagonists featured. Out of old antagonists, I'd suspect Kerberoi, Cthonian and enemy Bound (the vacant, wretched, krewe rivalry, forceful krewes like the Sacrosanct, or just malicious ones that want your stuff). As far as new antagonists go there ghosts that wear masks and ones that once you find out about them, they find out about you, which may or may not be one in the same. Deathlords are no longer a thing are in their place are Cthonic Gods, whether antagonistic or not. Might be more new antagonists but guess we'll have to find out in later spoilers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T06:33:48-07:00","id":1109211,"title":"","content":"Has anyone seen the anime Le Chevalier D'Eon? The main character is a soldier whose murdered sister's ghost bonds to him as he's been attacked by a sorcery tainted horror. I haven't seen the whole thing, but in Geist terms it looks like his is Bound to his sister's ghost and their keystone is her crucifix. She can fully take over their shared body, changing it into her own form. any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T19:51:22-07:00","id":1109557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1108359#post1108359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure one of the new antagonist types is a variety of Bound who have taken on cthonians rather than geister</div> </div> </div> </div> Why are sure of that? Just curious, sounds interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T22:31:15-07:00","id":1109633,"title":"","content":"It's been hinted at here and there, and is compiled into the original post of this thread. While I wasn't that familiar with first edition, it seems that this time around there's more emphasis on playing <i>the Bound</i> rather than playing a <i>Sin-eater</i>. The latter might be the default protagonists but it seems they're emphasizing that there's a difference between what actually <i>is</i> bound to you.<br /> <br /> To me that implies there's some scary shit out there making their own Bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T09:17:41-07:00","id":1109785,"title":"","content":"Well with Cthonians being native to the Underworld it does raise the question of what happens when they enter the world of the living, against their will or otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T09:33:05-07:00","id":1109792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1109785#post1109785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well with Cthonians being native to the Underworld it does raise the question of what happens when they enter the world of the living, against their will or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing various flavors of &quot;bad&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T18:22:01-07:00","id":1109987,"title":"","content":"Very bad for anyone crossing paths with a Cthonian. I definitely have a feeling Cthonian Bound would fall under antagonists, perhaps equivalent to a Mad Abyssal Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T19:54:42-07:00","id":1110018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1109633#post1109633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been hinted at here and there, and is compiled into the original post of this thread. While I wasn't that familiar with first edition, it seems that this time around there's more emphasis on playing <i>the Bound</i> rather than playing a <i>Sin-eater</i>. The latter might be the default protagonists but it seems they're emphasizing that there's a difference between what actually <i>is</i> bound to you.<br /> <br /> To me that implies there's some scary shit out there making their own Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>The term Sin-Eater doesn't have to do with what bound you though, it's &quot;Now that I'm bound I spend my time freeing ghosts from their anchors&quot;. There is no reason a Cthonic-Bound would have any difficultly being a Sin-Eater over a Geist-Bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T20:00:30-07:00","id":1110022,"title":"","content":"That's fine; I just meant 'Sin-eater' as 'someone bound to a geist' in order to distinguish it from someone bound to a cthonian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T23:20:12-07:00","id":1110074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1110022#post1110022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine; I just meant 'Sin-eater' as 'someone bound to a geist' in order to distinguish it from someone bound to a cthonian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. I'm saying that terminology is incorrect and shouldn't be used to try and infer information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T04:41:14-07:00","id":1115878,"title":"","content":"Have they had the kick starter if Geist: The Sin-Eaters 2e yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","titl