of any direct connection to the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T12:01:47-07:00","id":1133105,"title":"","content":"Well, geists aren't anchored to concepts either anymore. They're just ghosts that have learned a specific Manifestation; the Bargain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T12:48:35-07:00","id":1133122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1133105#post1133105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, geists aren't anchored to concepts either anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=960561#post960561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geists are Rank 3+ ghosts. The only (well, almost only) way for a ghost to cross from Rank 2 to Rank 3 is to drink deep from one of the rivers of the Underworld. This does... strange things to the shade brave/desperate enough to try it--but it does mean <b>they're Anchored to a <i>concept</i> of death,</b> which makes it much harder for them to get blasted back to the Underworld once they escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T14:24:48-07:00","id":1133161,"title":"","content":"Yes. They may be ghosts, but ghosts need a leg-up to get above Rank 2 and they're not 'just ghosts' at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T14:34:15-07:00","id":1133167,"title":"","content":"Ah. I must've missed that. However it applies to all ghosts so it wouldn't change geists into half-spirits anymore than it would any ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T18:23:50-07:00","id":1133243,"title":"","content":"Plus it's &quot;anchored to a concept of Death&quot; not just &quot;anchored to a concept&quot;, so Death would obviously still be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T18:57:54-07:00","id":1133250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1133243#post1133243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus it's &quot;anchored to a concept of Death&quot; not just &quot;anchored to a concept&quot;, so <b>Death would obviously still be enough</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not remotely the metaphysical quagmire I'm addressing by pointing out that requiring Spirit to affect wouldn't necessitate a geist be part spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T22:01:30-07:00","id":1133283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1133250#post1133250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not remotely the metaphysical quagmire I'm addressing by pointing out that requiring Spirit to affect wouldn't necessitate a geist be part spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't replying to you. I just saying you obviously wouldn't need a different Arcana to effect a ghost just because it has more Death put into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T07:12:33-07:00","id":1133776,"title":"","content":"I don't know where to place ideas I think would really make Geist cool at least for me<br /> <br /> Make it so Geist enjoy living so much that they not only come back from the dead but can act like reapers as a temptation. When they reap someone they get that persons life added to them. They can take years from people and give it to others if they want.<br /> <br /> Now this is where the saying &quot;You reap what you sow&quot; comes in. Keep killing to live longer rather then just living out your years with the second chance you got. Bad things happen, some times you get not only haunted by the ghosts of your past but some of these ghosts seek revenge. Ask yourself what happens when your victims become a geist and come after you or the people you love. Going full dark just taking lives for fun your key become a scythe<br /> <br /> Now I know some Geists might find away around this to live longer such as taking lives of people in combat but maybe their should be a ritual you have to do on your key before you reap or maybe you can only reap to the type of death that is attuned to your key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 08-25-2017, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:22:02-07:00","id":1133791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1133776#post1133776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know where to place ideas I think would really make Geist cool at least for me<br /> <br /> Make it so Geist enjoy living so much that they not only come back from the dead but can act like reapers as a temptation. When they reap someone they get that persons life added to them. They can take years from people and give it to others if they want.<br /> <br /> Now this is where the saying &quot;You reap what you sow&quot; Keep killing to live longer rather then just living out your years with the second chance you got some times these ghosts seek revenge, what happens when your victims become a geist and come after you or the people you love. Going full dark just taking lives for fun and rather then having a Key you are now considered to have a \u200bscythe.<br /> <br /> Now I know some Geists might find away around this to live longer such as taking lives of people in combat but maybe their should be a ritual you have to do on your key before you reap or maybe you can only reap to the type of death that is attuned to your key.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool thoughts! There is going to be some type of being called Reapers in Geist 2E (based on the spoiler blubs from Dark Eras 2 World War I era), but they could very well be the non-Sin-eater Bound who glut on stolen life as you suggest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:28:02-07:00","id":1133793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1133283#post1133283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't replying to you. I just saying you obviously wouldn't need a different Arcana to effect a ghost just because it has more Death put into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't you still need Spirit for spirits of death? I'm not saying that I couldn't see the justification for Death alone, but if anchoring them to a concept of death makes them part spirit, then it might still require both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:42:43-07:00","id":1133803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1133793#post1133793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't you still need Spirit for spirits of death? I'm not saying that I couldn't see the justification for Death alone, but if anchoring them to a concept of death makes them part spirit, then it might still require both.</div> </div> </div> </div>The notion I was forwarding was more specifically that Resonance is within the purview of the Spirit Arcanum but has no necessary implication of being part spirit; the only direct interaction the Death Arcanum has with Resonance thusfar relates to opening an Avernian Gate, and that's a rather more broad-scale Resonant tag than &quot;Death by Fire&quot; or &quot;Death by Hanging&quot; or &quot;Death by Murder.&quot;<br /> <br /> Spells like Corpse Mask can alter the apparent cause of death for a body, but in general it's not difficult to extrapolate the Moros's smaller rapport with the Underworld relative to the Thyrsus's influence on the Shadow into a necessary buffer between Death magic and the wider/more esoteric ecosystems of the Great Below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T09:38:52-07:00","id":1133834,"title":"","content":"There are several rotes in the MtAw 2E corebook that are Death, Spirit, or Mind Specific to effect ghosts, spirits, or goetia respectively, but still have the (along with 2-5 dots in Death will also effect ghosts or in Mind will also effect Goetia, or in Spirit will also effect spirits). In my musings I just treat the Geist like a ghost. the Death specific rotes effect them normally. the rotes that say (add Death 2-5 dots to effect ghosts, would effect Geists when the Death dots and the spirit or mind dots are at the right level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:32:39-07:00","id":1133884,"title":"","content":"Well if we're talking about neat ideas that we'd like to see, I think it would be neat to have the spectres of those whose lives have been cut short because of your Geist to bring you back again after your initial death be a topic. Shadowy phantoms that stare a distance that stand out from the other ghosts you can see. Ones that know you are to blame for their forced fate and are an obstacle to them moving on. In 1e you see the life of the person that died flash before your eyes so I'd like to believe it opens up a connection when you take their life force and it's a two way street that they can see out of. I imagine one could make for a particularly emotional or spiteful antagonist that keeps its distance from you and tries to ruin your life or hurt your loved ones as punishment for taking it's life.<br /> <br /> ...if this ends up being those ghosts with masks or the antagonist teased that knows about you when you know about it then I'll jump with joy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T15:37:54-07:00","id":1133968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1133884#post1133884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if we're talking about neat ideas that we'd like to see, I think it would be neat to have the spectres of those whose lives have been cut short because of your Geist to bring you back again after your initial death be a topic. Shadowy phantoms that stare a distance that stand out from the other ghosts you can see. Ones that know you are to blame for their forced fate and are an obstacle to them moving on. In 1e you see the life of the person that died flash before your eyes so I'd like to believe it opens up a connection when you take their life force and it's a two way street that they can see out of. I imagine one could make for a particularly emotional or spiteful antagonist that keeps its distance from you and tries to ruin your life or hurt your loved ones as punishment for taking it's life.<br /> <br /> ...if this ends up being those ghosts with masks or the antagonist teased that knows about you when you know about it then I'll jump with joy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I wrote a Geist Plot Hook about something similar to this. Very Planescape: Torment-y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T22:22:43-07:00","id":1134054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1133793#post1133793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't you still need Spirit for spirits of death? I'm not saying that I couldn't see the justification for Death alone, but if anchoring them to a concept of death makes them part spirit, then it might still require both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except there is more mention of spirits of death. It's literally Ghost + More Death Symbols. There is no reason to assume that would give them Spirit symbols.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T12:12:14-07:00","id":1134213,"title":"","content":"hmm... if sin eaters still sacrifice people when they receive followup resurrections (which i hope is elaborated on more, does the geist need to leave the body to do this? range limit?) could the ghosts of those sacrificed come back to haunt the sin eater, perhaps as dangerous spirits rather than normal confused ghosts. It'd be neat if the ghosts of those sacrificed were noted antagonists, similar to the mekhet's shadow in requiem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 08-26-2017, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T11:41:05-07:00","id":1138654,"title":"","content":"So... Is there any news about the book? Any date for an Open Development blog?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":".  Typos 09-08-2017, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T13:00:08-07:00","id":1138680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1134213#post1134213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm... if sin eaters still sacrifice people when they receive followup resurrections (which i hope is elaborated on more, does the geist need to leave the body to do this? range limit?) could the ghosts of those sacrificed come back to haunt the sin eater, perhaps as dangerous spirits rather than normal confused ghosts. It'd be neat if the ghosts of those sacrificed were noted antagonists, similar to the mekhet's shadow in requiem</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually sounds a bit intriguing! So...being haunted by your choices and the price to pay for returning back...sounds like it would absolutely fit well in this type of game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T13:04:23-07:00","id":1138682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EldritchMinister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1138680#post1138680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This actually sounds a bit intriguing! So...being haunted by your choices and the price to pay for returning back...sounds like it would absolutely fit well in this type of game!</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't lie the idea came from the Tithed ones in the time of reckoning scenarios for CtD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T04:18:32-07:00","id":1138844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1138654#post1138654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Is there any news about the book? Any date for an Open Development blog?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not heard a thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T18:47:23-07:00","id":1140692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1134213#post1134213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm... if sin eaters still sacrifice people when they receive followup resurrections (which i hope is elaborated on more, does the geist need to leave the body to do this? range limit?) could the ghosts of those sacrificed come back to haunt the sin eater, perhaps as dangerous spirits rather than normal confused ghosts. It'd be neat if the ghosts of those sacrificed were noted antagonists, similar to the mekhet's shadow in requiem</div> </div> </div> </div>It reminds me of Echoes from Demon: The Descent, not that that's a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T19:21:04-07:00","id":1140696,"title":"","content":"This might be abit off topic, but whenever i read stuff about the Bargain, i get the feeling that it could work (with some tweaks) with demon style or inferno style spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T02:47:57-07:00","id":1144320,"title":"","content":"It's been a few days since there was a post here, so I thought I'd stir the pot. Thresholds seemed a solid x-splat concept in 1e and it has been mentioned that they will have more mechanical relevance in 2e. What about y-splat? the 1e y-splat (archetype) i never liked as much as thresholds, and I'm hoping we'll see a new one with the 1e archetypes making the anchors of 2e. any thoughts on y-splat possibilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T10:10:10-07:00","id":1144476,"title":"","content":"When I did a 1.5e patch to use geist in a 2e mage game, what I did was treat the Archetypes the same as demon's Agendas, and that worked rather well. Made a neat condition for my Necromancer PC.<br /> <br /> It's tough because GtSE emphasized personal experiences and self determination. Krewes are basically &quot;build your own mystery cult&quot;. So it made sense for the Y Splat to be how the character deals with their second chance (or at least the ghosty business parts). You can't really have large organizations like the other Y Splats without really cutting into those themes. So, you look at Demon and Promethean for &quot;now be be&quot; personal philosophies. And I think Geists archetypes were actually pretty solid from that perspective. There's obviously more they can do with it, but completely changing it... I don't know where to go with that without undercutting some of the core themes.<br /> But I'm curious what others think!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T09:49:37-07:00","id":1154417,"title":"","content":"As per MM notes, it looks like we get a Geist preview this week. Hopefully today, since that would be thematically appropriate.","signa