blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T06:40:33-07:00","id":1154690,"title":"","content":"Great stuff teased. Looks like reapers are one of the new antagonists after all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T06:44:37-07:00","id":1154692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154690#post1154690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great stuff teased. Looks like reapers are one of the new antagonists after all!</div> </div> </div> </div>It almost seems like the overarching antagonist is now the Underworld itself. Which is going to be really interesting once we get the three Geist eras in DE2, especially Scandenavian Witch Trials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T07:04:36-07:00","id":1154698,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting that the game seems to be positing the Chthonic Gods as a slightly more present version of the Deathlords, as if they're things you can charge down into the Dead Dominions and challenge. Catabasis is a descent, and usually a <i>return</i> to the land of the living, one that gives knowledge or power, and it sounds sort of like that would be the Sin-Eater equivalent to Archmastery. Descend to the Depths, become a Chthonic God, reshape the Great Below in your image.<br /> <br /> Also, did anyone notice that Sin-Eaters seem to be getting a Going Loud equivalent in unleashing their Geist? Sounds like it would be terrifying, considering Geists are Rank 3+ ghosts, and stats-wise those beings are hardly slouches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T07:49:01-07:00","id":1154707,"title":"","content":"So it sounds like they are keeping the initial Manifestations (renamed to Haunts) from 1E, though I thought they were restructuring how they worked? The &quot;baseline effect at 1 dot&quot; matches 1E. I'm curious how they are going to break the Grid Dependency, though. Maybe not all the Keys have their effects listed for each Haunt?<br /> <br /> So, they <i>are</i> going with &quot;Why are you back&quot; as a major motivation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T07:50:11-07:00","id":1154708,"title":"","content":"Oh my Gods, this preview is awesome! There is not a single thing I read in it that I didn't adore. From what I've seen, I love the Burdens. Interestingly enough, the Abiding sound similar to a homebrew Beast Hunger I've been working on. I can't wait to see how Thresholds get folded into Keys. It'll be interesting to see how necromancers differ from from the necromantic members of other splats, and how the new Underworld is going to work. I honestly can't decide which of the options I hope wins the vote for next time, as both sound fascinating. Most of all, I'm glad that Geists will have more teeth this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T09:36:48-07:00","id":1154743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154692#post1154692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It almost seems like the overarching antagonist is now the Underworld itself. Which is going to be really interesting once we get the three Geist eras in DE2, especially Scandenavian Witch Trials.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds almost like a more Gothic Godmachine figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T10:38:56-07:00","id":1154763,"title":"","content":"All personal opinion ahead.<br /> <br /> I'm...trying to be open to the new Burdens, but they feel rather more limiting for creating a character concept than the Thresholds were. The Thresholds were very easy to tailor to any given situation, and they were highly archetypal and elemental, covering all the different ways a person could die. Burdens, from their descriptions, seem like you have to figure out how to stick your character in one of 5 somewhat rigid categories. They feel to Thresholds how oWoD Natures/Demeanors feel to CoD 2e Virtues/Vices. That being said, this was a tiny preview and I know I'll have to see a better outline before I understand how it'll really work.<br /> <br /> On the same vein, Burdens make Sin-Eaters feel more like ephemeral entities than full people. The limited categorizing of their motivations for coming back feels like the way ghosts are written up, where ephemeral entities have certain things they pursue and don't really experience the dynamic aspects of life outside of that. That said, it seems like the effect is intended. After reading the whole preview, I believe that may be what the devs are going for with 2e, especially taken together with the Catharsis endgame possibility and previous comments from devs about how 2e Sin-Eaters do not in fact have souls.<br /> <br /> So given my personal tastes, those things I'm not really hyped over, but from an objective standpoint this all seems to be coming together nicely, fits together nicely, and I really like basically everything else that was mentioned in the preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:28:57-07:00","id":1154782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154763#post1154763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All personal opinion ahead.<br /> <br /> I'm...trying to be open to the new Burdens, but they feel rather more limiting for creating a character concept than the Thresholds were. The Thresholds were very easy to tailor to any given situation, and they were highly archetypal and elemental, covering all the different ways a person could die. Burdens, from their descriptions, seem like you have to figure out how to stick your character in one of 5 somewhat rigid categories. They feel to Thresholds how oWoD Natures/Demeanors feel to CoD 2e Virtues/Vices. That being said, this was a tiny preview and I know I'll have to see a better outline before I understand how it'll really work.<br /> <br /> On the same vein, Burdens make Sin-Eaters feel more like ephemeral entities than full people. The limited categorizing of their motivations for coming back feels like the way ghosts are written up, where ephemeral entities have certain things they pursue and don't really experience the dynamic aspects of life outside of that. That said, it seems like the effect is intended. After reading the whole preview, I believe that may be what the devs are going for with 2e, especially taken together with the Catharsis endgame possibility and previous comments from devs about how 2e Sin-Eaters do not in fact have souls.<br /> <br /> So given my personal tastes, those things I'm not really hyped over, but from an objective standpoint this all seems to be coming together nicely, fits together nicely, and I really like basically everything else that was mentioned in the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're coming from, with Burdens making them seem more like ghosts. That makes sense to me, though, given that I believe it's been said that it's the ghost that makes the Bargain with the Geist. I'd imagine that those probably aren't the only Burdens that exist, though. There are probably others that might show up in a Players Guide in the future. I'm curious, though, what kind of individuals would you see as being unrepresented by the available choices? The only ones that have occurred to me so far would be the Frightened, those that can't let themselves rest because they are too terrified of what awaits them on the other side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:30:31-07:00","id":1154783,"title":"","content":"Very excited about the new post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll be updating the initial post today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:30:49-07:00","id":1154784,"title":"","content":"For me, 1E suffered from the degree to which it played like the Bound were just humans who are now immortal because it turned out dying was the key to getting cool powers (don\u2019t get me wrong - I like cool powers!). Now it reads like the game about playing a desperate ghost who has made a bargain (with actual trade-offs) to return to life! So this is a change I am in favor of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:35:20-07:00","id":1154805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154763#post1154763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm...trying to be open to the new Burdens, but they feel rather more limiting for creating a character concept than the Thresholds were. The Thresholds were very easy to tailor to any given situation, and they were highly archetypal and elemental, covering all the different ways a person could die. Burdens, from their descriptions, seem like you have to figure out how to stick your character in one of 5 somewhat rigid categories.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be a common theme with second edition. In 1e, most gamelines' various splats were a set of archetypes, into which you could fit just about any character concept. 2e is moving towards giving the splats more specific meaning within the setting. It'll be interesting to see if the reaction to this is as negative for Geist as it was for Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:07:30-07:00","id":1154816,"title":"","content":"I'm very fired up for this, it sounds great, and like a fulfillment of Geist. I think this is one of the 2e's I've most been looking forward to, because it was both easy and hard to imagine what a cleaned up Geist would be like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:14:50-07:00","id":1154819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154805#post1154805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to be a common theme with second edition. In 1e, most gamelines' various splats were a set of archetypes, into which you could fit just about any character concept. 2e is moving towards giving the splats more specific meaning within the setting. It'll be interesting to see if the reaction to this is as negative for Geist as it was for Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Geist 1E had a lot less material built up and published for fans to get attached to than Changeling 1E, which had 6 full supplement books and a time setting for Victorian England. It may be that the lack of world building Geist 1E had compared to earlier 1E Chronicle of Darkness lines will mean that there is a lot more room to fill in themes and focus for the line and will have less of an entrenched opinion (for or against the proposed changes) than the Changeling 2E reactions had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:22:00-07:00","id":1154824,"title":"","content":"I mean the burdens don't seem that restrictive, sure not not as open as 'the way that you died' but still pretty flexible.<br /> <br /> TBH I'm more interested in the new Krewe Stuff, really liking the look of necropolitans and undertakers.<br /> and the short section on end game stuff, the catharsis end game looks to really drive home the ghostyness of bound, and well catabasis sounds a lot like archmastery and i like the sound of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T14:10:55-07:00","id":1154838,"title":"","content":"The only thing Burdens conceptually marginalize that would have been a thing in 1E is someone who (to quote someone in my group who is iffy on the changes) &quot;just doesn't want to be dead&quot;. There's definitely a stronger sense now that the Bound need to be particularly driven to live for some reason - that the Geists don't offer the Bargain to anyone who who meets the metaphysical requirements at random (woudn't be surprised if the &quot;touched by death/otherworldly-sight/etc before&quot; requirement isn't there anymore). Just wanting to live isn't enough, you need to want SOMETHING.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T14:22:13-07:00","id":1154842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154838#post1154838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing Burdens conceptually marginalize that would have been a thing in 1E is someone who (to quote someone in my group who is iffy on the changes) &amp;quot;just doesn't want to be dead&amp;quot;. There's definitely a stronger sense now that the Bound need to be particularly driven to live for some reason - that the Geists don't offer the Bargain to anyone who who meets the metaphysical requirements at random (woudn't be surprised if the &amp;quot;touched by death/otherworldly-sight/etc before&amp;quot; requirement isn't there anymore). Just wanting to live isn't enough, you need to want SOMETHING.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, you could say the human just didn\u2019t want to be dead, and the burden is the Geist\u2019s reason for wanting to come back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T14:24:08-07:00","id":1154843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154842#post1154842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, you could say the human just didn\u2019t want to be dead, and the burden is the Geist\u2019s reason for wanting to come back.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That definitely doesn't seem to be the case currently. These are distinctly human motivations, and Geists (based on the catharsis description) are detached from their humanity. Their reason to want to come back will presumably be the other side of the Bargain, and likely involve being incarnations of death itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T14:29:37-07:00","id":1154844,"title":"","content":"I like the burdens conceptually but I worry they will be resolved too easily without the storyteller bending over backwards to draw out the goal. All of the burdens have a clearly defined goal that realistically would not take long to resolve in most cases. Avenging your own murder is a great example: take 'The Crow' for instance, dude comes back with a bird spirit (aka a geist in this game) and hunts down his murderers, whole thing took about 2-3 days. While some issues will take longer, resolving those situations for other ghosts is the main theme of the game so you'll have alot of practice when you do it for yourself...and then what? Sure you need to resolve your geist's issues before you can move on but your character's main motivation has been resolved<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm overthinking it since we don't see as much of sin eater society, it could be that finding yourself after this resolution is a big thing and the main reasons krews form in the first place. Okay i'm done... now what?... I know I'll be a spooky ghost person! It just seems that doing that would be like making changeling types based around a fetch. An important part of the character sure but not one that will last the entire chronicle nine times out of ten and not for every player. Hoping to see the next preview address this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T14:40:20-07:00","id":1154848,"title":"","content":"well, Geist's preview seems to be <i>really</i> interesting. Having 2E featuring the &quot;Chronicles of the Dead&quot; gives a great flavor for that edition, and it looks like it manage to capture Geist's essence as a game between life, death and second chances- especially the way the Burdens are being presented. I must say that I do feel some sorrow for the loss of Thresholds, but Burdens work so perfectly that the chances are that if they were used in the previous Edition I would have never felt that sense of loss- they are just so natural. Perhaps the core concept could be used for an homebrew &quot;wraith&quot; splat. We'll see.<br /> <br /> As for the antagonists- the Reapers seems to remind me a antagonist concept I've had for ages, even though I've pictured those antagonists as the emissaries of the Kerebros instead of the Deathloths/Chthonic Gods. I do like the more active role the Chthonic Gods take in the setting. I also how different they would end up from the Chthonians (I think they are not the same kind of entity, but right now I'm not sure). I wonder if the mention of &quot;ghosts wearing masks&quot; was about the Reapers, or about the eaters of the dead. Also, the greater emphasis which the game puts on non Sin Eater Bounds and small things like &quot;River Cities&quot; makes me really excited. It looks like that like the supernatural creature it represents, Geist as died and returned to get a second chance, making it (as it seems) the game which was changed the most from the transition to the new edition.<br /> <br /> In sort, all of that makes me really excited toward the new edition- heck there is even a chance that Geist may take Hunter's place as my most favorite gameline (a small chance, and a lot depends on how the editions would turn out- but not a negligible one, either)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T14:41:43-07:00","id":1154849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154844#post1154844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the burdens conceptually but I worry they will be resolved too easily without the storyteller bending over backwards to draw out the goal. All of the burdens have a clearly defined goal that realistically would not take long to resolve in most cases. Avenging your own murder is a great example: take 'The Crow' for instance, dude comes back with a bird spirit (aka a geist in this game) and hunts down his murderers, whole thing took about 2-3 days. While some issues will take longer, resolving those situations for other ghosts is the main theme of the game so you'll have alot of practice when you do it for yourself...and then what? Sure you need to resolve your geist's issues before you can move on but your character's main motivation has been resolved<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm overthinking it since we don't see as much of sin eater society, it could be that finding yourself after this resolution is a big thing and the main reasons krews form in the first place. Okay i'm done... now what?... I know I'll be a spooky ghost person! It just seems that doing that would be like making changeling types based around a fetch. An important part of the character sure but not one that will last the entire chronicle nine times out of ten and not for every player. Hoping to see the next preview address this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, you'll find out that your Burden doesn't end where you think it does - track down your murderer and you'll find it doesn't satisfy like you thought it would, and there is more to do. The ones you come back to protect expand beyond the first. There is always more stuff you can't bring with you. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T14:55:01-07:00","id":1154850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154849#post1154849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably, you'll find out that your Burden doesn't end where you think it does - track down your murderer and you'll find it doesn't satisfy like you thought it would, and there is more to do. The ones you come back to protect expand beyond the first. There is always more stuff you can't bring with you. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is sort of how ghosts work. You go back to kill the counselors who were fooling around instead of caring out for you. Then other counselors whenever they're fooling around, though I know that in the movies that's more of a slasher. You come back to ensure your apartment building gets finished then linger around to make sure the people who stay there aren't reprehensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T15:09:58-07:00","id":1154854,"title":"","content":"Also, Katharsis endgame points out you need to resolve Burden AND find lost humanity of your Geist. If resolving Burden can be rather simple - finding humanity of Geist I think will be rather problematic... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T15:18:37-07:00","id":1154856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154854#post1154854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Katharsis endgame points out you need to resolve Burden AND find lost humanity of your Geist. If resolving Burden can be rather simple - finding humanity of Geist I think will be rather problematic... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree that there is more stuff you CAN do but based on just the preview most players i've played with would feel rather lost after completing their burden assuming that it's meant to be a major character motivation. It's the central reason they came back and now that it's done their character would lack direction. They COULD oppose the underworld or resolve their geists anchors but would they WANT to. They had a mission and now it's done. My worry isn't that there isn't more to do my worry is that the players will be given an objective, make it their central motivation and then feel lost when it's done. I'd like to see more about sin eaters and their beliefs previewed so i know where to take the game once their burden is resolved since it can't stay a motivation for long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T15:44:10-07:00","id":1154862,"title":"","content":"Just not wanting to die is a basic qualification for all of these Burdens. The supposition that the Burdens seem to offer is that there's always a <i>why</i> that's more sophisticated than just wanting to live, which is something I arguably agree with. Why do you want to keep living? Everyone has an answer more specific than just wanting to live, even if all they can manage in the moment is that they don't want to die.<br /> <br /> Maybe your 1e Sin-Eater who didn't want to die just came back, but whatever they did once they got back is probably suggestive of what their Burden actually was.<br /> <br /> Like, wild guess... I think a lot of people who just &quot;don't want to die&quot; probably fall under the Abiding, the Hungry or the Kindly Burdens.<br /> <br /> I was initially just gonna say the Hungry, and I contend that most of the motivations you'd think of probably fall under it. &quot;I have more countries to see! More food to eat! More life to live! I don't wanna die!&quot; et al.<br /> <br /> It's a weird shift to from a question which is reactive in nature to a proactive one, but I'm certain that it wouldn't actually be hard to address any first edition Geist character in this second edition framework in a compelling way.<br /> <br /> It's also possible that this might enhance a character by providing them with a greater motivating force than in First Edition, since I recall &quot;What's my motivation?&quot; being a consistent criticism of Geist 1e. :P<br /> <br /> An interesting thought: Your Burden might be more honest than you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 11-01-2017, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T16:02:06-07:00","id":1154870,"title":"","content":"Trying to think of a Sin-Eater which doesn't fit into the Burdens seems pretty difficult considering you have to have had a ghost before you can become Bound and it'd be weird for a ghost to not have fit into one of the burdens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T17:40:56-07:00","id":1154895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154870#post1154870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to think of a Sin-Eater which doesn't fit into the Burdens seems pretty difficult considering you have to have had a ghost before you can become Bound and it'd be weird for a ghost to not have fit into one of the burdens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I, personally, just liked the name Threshold as opposed to Burden, and I'm wondering which (if any) Horseman they now map to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T17:52:35-07:00","id":1154903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154782#post1154782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see where you're coming from, with Burdens making them seem more like ghosts. That makes sense to me, though, given that I believe it's been said that it's the ghost that makes the Bargain with the Geist. I'd imagine that those probably aren't the only Burdens that exist, though. There are probably others that might show up in a Players Guide in the future. I'm curious, though, what kind of individuals would you see as being unrepresented by the available choices? The only ones that have occurred to me so far would be the Frightened, those that can't let themselves rest because they are too terrified of what awaits them on the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it's more this than anything:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154844#post1154844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the burdens conceptually but I worry they will be resolved too easily without the storyteller bending over backwards to draw out the goal. All of the burdens have a clearly defined goal that realistically would not take long to resolve in most cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>CoD already has an Aspirations system. Making Burdens the place where the splat starts seems to suggest that Sin-Eaters don't have much depth beyond whatever drives them to stay on this side of the grave. In 1e, the character determined the Threshold, but here it sounds like the Burden will determine the character.<br /> <br /> As for additional Burdens, I understand the concept of forcing Bound to have specific reasons for wanting to come back rather than an open-ended &quot;just don't want to die yet,&quot; but really that is a very valid thing that could drive someone to want to live. As a name, I suppose it could be called the Unfulfilled, those who regret not being able to experience everything life has to offer, but a problem I already see there is that it doesn't fit in with the other kinds of &quot;drives&quot; Burdens give. It's not a purpose to complete, because the act of living itself becomes the purpose. It goes beyond Hungry, because Hungry limits itself to a single anchor of some kind. This is what I mean that it feels limiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":12708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","user":"Chesh","date":". 11-01-2017, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:32:45-07:00","id":1154922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154856#post1154856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't disagree that there is more stuff you CAN do but based on just the preview most players i've played with would feel rather lost after completing their burden assuming that it's meant to be a major character motivation. It's the central reason they came back and now that it's done their character would lack direction. They COULD oppose the underworld or resolve their geists anchors but would they WANT to. They had a mission and now it's done. My worry isn't that there isn't more to do my worry is that the players will be given an objective, make it their central motivation and then feel lost when it's done. I'd like to see more about sin eaters and their beliefs previewed so i know where to take the game once their burden is resolved since it can't stay a motivation for long.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not all Burdens are solvable, some are eternal. And not all Sin Eaters would look at their Burdens as something to resolve, many who look at those Burdens as something to cherish. <br /> <br /> I don't think all Sin Eaters need an end game, for some it's enough to simply enjoy the life that was, almost stolen from you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:59:45-07:00","id":1154927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154922#post1154922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not all Burdens are solvable, some are eternal. And not all Sin Eaters would look at their Burdens as something to resolve, many who look at those Burdens as something to cherish. <br /> <br /> I don't think all Sin Eaters need an end game, for some it's enough to simply enjoy the life that was, almost stolen from you.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Hungry, that could be the whole point. They died realizing their life was over before it began, and return wanting a full life. A person who dies and comes back purely because they didn't feel like dying yet comes off as also Hungry-their Burden is to not waste it, because the kind of willpower that cheats death simply by survival instinct is someone following their desire for more life to its natural conclusion.<br /> <br /> On the Horsemen, if they remain A Thing:<br /> <br /> Conquest: Abiding (&quot;So help me god, I will not rest until I have done something worthwhile).<br /> <br /> War: Vengeance (duh)<br /> <br /> Famine: Hungry (more duh)<br /> <br /> Death: Bereaved (marked by him twice over, in fact)<br /> <br /> Hades: Kindly (Hell has come to account for sins)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T19:04:31-07:00","id":1154930,"title":"","content":"I never liked the horsemen thing because of how they made a 5th one come out of nowhere (plus I always prefer the Conquest interpretation over the Pestilence interpretation). Could change them to be Cthonic Gods in 2e I suppose though, so that they actually exist as figures you can interact with rather than it just being &quot;each x splat is associated with a horseman and that's the only time they're ever discussed&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154903#post1154903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for additional Burdens, I understand the concept of forcing Bound to have specific reasons for wanting to come back rather than an open-ended &quot;just don't want to die yet,&quot; but really that is a very valid thing that could drive someone to want to live.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except individuals like that would never have left a ghost to begin with, so it's impossible for such people to become a 2e bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-01-2017, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T19:05:33-07:00","id":1154931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154927#post1154927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Horsemen, if they remain A Thing:</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=969059#post969059\">It doesn't sound like it.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154930#post1154930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except individuals like that would never have left a ghost to begin with, so it's impossible for such people to become a 2e bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair there's a load of things in Chronicles that could have made a ghost beyond the burdens. A mage can, for instance, just make a ghost out of nothing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-01-2017, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T19:40:29-07:00","id":1154940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154931#post1154931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair there's a load of things in Chronicles that could have made a ghost beyond the burdens. A mage can, for instance, just make a ghost out of nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they wouldn't be able to be a bound either because they didn't die and have no body to go to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T19:48:01-07:00","id":1154945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154940#post1154940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they wouldn't be able to be a bound either because they didn't die and have no body to go to.</div> </div> </div> </div>A ghost makes a Bargain with a dying or dead human. The human doesn't seem to die and become their own geist.<br /> <br /> More effort seems to be in the geists hands than the human, even if the humans want can interest the ghost to begin with.<br /> <br /> Or are you just referring to the dying human? I'm thinking Bound refers to the combination, not one side, is that incorrect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-01-2017, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:06:59-07:00","id":1154949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154945#post1154945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A ghost makes a Bargain with a dying or dead human. The human doesn't seem to die and become their own geist.<br /> <br /> More effort seems to be in the geists hands than the human, even if the humans want can interest the ghost to begin with.<br /> <br /> Or are you just referring to the dying human? I'm thinking Bound refers to the combination, not one side, is that incorrect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about the geist, I am talking about the dying human. It has been said that in 2e the geist makes a deal with the ghost of the person who died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:13:30-07:00","id":1154953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154949#post1154949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has been said that in 2e the geist makes a deal with the ghost of the person who died.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting that from?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition#post1032849\">Robert D seems to have gathered the information about it</a> and it still seems about the ghost offering the Bargain, then becoming a geist. They do answer my Bound terminology question, though.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing information about the dead persons ghost. It seems a convoluted way to go about things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:27:26-07:00","id":1154959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154953#post1154953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are you getting that from?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition#post1032849\">Robert D seems to have gathered the information about it</a> and it still seems about the ghost offering the Bargain, then becoming a geist. They do answer my Bound terminology question, though.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing information about the dead persons ghost. It seems a convoluted way to go about things.</div> </div> </div> </div>While i'm uncertain about the ghost of the person who died (though that would make sense given the way sin-eaters are being portrayed) at no point in geist has a ghost become geist through the bargain. The bargain is a unique ability of geists (a specific manifestation in 2e I believe) and the process of becoming a geist was vague and mysterious in 1e (though it was implied they were a magath) and 2e has mentioned that ghosts become geists by drinking from the rivers of the underworld","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:37:02-07:00","id":1154964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154953#post1154953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you getting that from?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was in a discussion about the sin-eater not having souls, and then there were some posts which implied that the dead person's ghost was the one involved in the bargain and that their &quot;sin-eater to be's&quot; ghost comes before their death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and it still seems about the ghost offering the Bargain, then becoming a geist. </div> </div> </div>That's not been said anywhere (not even the Robert D post). The geist is a geist long before they make the bargain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not seeing information about the dead persons ghost. It seems a convoluted way to go about things. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it's convoluted? You die, now you're a ghost. Geist makes bargain with your ghost. You're now one of the bound.<br /> <br /> Plus it would actually explain how the geist can talk to you after your dead, otherwise there is no way for them to actually attempt the bargain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-01-2017, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:40:55-07:00","id":1154968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154959#post1154959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While i'm uncertain about the ghost of the person who died (though that would make sense given the way sin-eaters are being portrayed) at no point in geist has a ghost become geist through the bargain. The bargain is a unique ability of geists (a specific manifestation in 2e I believe) and the process of becoming a geist was vague and mysterious in 1e (though it was implied they were a magath) and 2e has mentioned that ghosts become geists by drinking from the rivers of the underworld</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, you're right, I was misremembering something Brookshaw said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1060949#post1060949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geists are a subset of Rank 3+ ghosts. It's as simple as a Geist is a ghost that has the Bargain Manifestation, whether or not she's used it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A geist is one that has the Bargain, not just one who uses it. You break the Rank 2 to 3 barrier by drinking from the rivers, or presumably some other magic influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154964#post1154964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how it's convoluted? You die, now you're a ghost. Geist makes bargain with your ghost. You're now one of the bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except there's also the step where your ghost is going back into your dead body and animating it and there's effectively two ghosts involved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus it would actually explain how the geist can talk to you after your dead, otherwise there is no way for them to actually attempt the bargain. </div> </div> </div>I was hoping it would be limited to dying, so you wouldn't have Bound that died 100 years ago. Though of course even afterward it doesn't seem like a stretch to say 'ghost magic,' since that's a conceit the rest of it seems based off of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-01-2017, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T21:05:31-07:00","id":1154975,"title":"","content":"After discussing with a friend, I fleshed out my distaste for the Burdens a bit more.<br /> <br /> I understand it's too early to really judge, and this has been a bare-bones preview for the splat. I will reel myself in after this and wait until we get more info before writing Burdens off. Taken in isolation with the language used, however, they make it sound like Burdens are a quest or an agenda, not a character aspect. For other splats, the starting points (clan, auspice, path, etc) are background aspects that influence a character's life just like any mortal background aspect, but it's not something that controls what they choose to do with their lives. A Nosferatu who wants revenge on his sire will still be a Nosferatu with all his Nosferatu-ness after that sire is dead, and he will still use all his Nosferatu-ness in whatever future endeavors he pursues, no matter how un-vengeful those ambitions end up being.<br /> <br /> What happens when a Bereaved finds that person they were looking for? What happens when a Kindly achieves justice for the wrong committed? What happens if the Hungry's anchor is destroyed? Do you pick a new Burden or are you forced into the passing-on endgame scenario? I really hope future previews expand more on Burdens as traits rather than goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T21:14:30-07:00","id":1154976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154968#post1154968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except there's also the step where your ghost is going back into your dead body and animating it and there's effectively two ghosts involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, since the &quot;ghost before you're actually dead&quot; bit means it never needs to have left your body. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was hoping it would be limited to dying, so you wouldn't have Bound that died 100 years ago. Though of course even afterward it doesn't seem like a stretch to say 'ghost magic,' since that's a conceit the rest of it seems based off of. </div> </div> </div>It is still limited to dying so I'm not sure what your talking about with this. Could you clarify on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T21:23:21-07:00","id":1154979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154976#post1154976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, since the &quot;ghost before you're actually dead&quot; bit means it never needs to have left your body.<br /> <br /> It is still limited to dying so I'm not sure what your talking about with this. Could you clarify on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically the ghost before you're dead part. Like I said, it happens, but generally the ghost thing seems to happen after a death, not during a dying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T21:24:19-07:00","id":1154980,"title":"","content":"Krewes ascending (descending?) to reshape the fundamental natuure of the Underworld was a headcanon I\u2019ve had for fucking ages now and I\u2019m very amused to see that made canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T21:48:10-07:00","id":1154982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154979#post1154979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically the ghost before you're dead part. Like I said, it happens, but generally the ghost thing seems to happen after a death, not during a dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the reason they can come into existence before persons actual death because of the whole &quot;ghosts are caused by the trauma and emotions which happen before death&quot; thing. I think Dave's even said somewhere that you can have situations messed up enough to spawn a ghost without you even dying at all. And then there are those things like ghosts of buildings and pens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-02-2017, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T01:37:45-07:00","id":1155000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154838#post1154838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing Burdens conceptually marginalize that would have been a thing in 1E is someone who (to quote someone in my group who is iffy on the changes) &quot;just doesn't want to be dead&quot;. There's definitely a stronger sense now that the Bound need to be particularly driven to live for some reason - that the Geists don't offer the Bargain to anyone who who meets the metaphysical requirements at random (woudn't be surprised if the &quot;touched by death/otherworldly-sight/etc before&quot; requirement isn't there anymore). Just wanting to live isn't enough, you need to want SOMETHING.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Just doesn't want to be dead&quot; is perhaps the most elemental expression of the Hungry burden--in essence, the thing you refuse to leave behind is <i>yourself</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154844#post1154844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the burdens conceptually but I worry they will be resolved too easily without the storyteller bending over backwards to draw out the goal. All of the burdens have a clearly defined goal that realistically would not take long to resolve in most cases. Avenging your own murder is a great example: take 'The Crow' for instance, dude comes back with a bird spirit (aka a geist in this game) and hunts down his murderers, whole thing took about 2-3 days. While some issues will take longer, resolving those situations for other ghosts is the main theme of the game so you'll have alot of practice when you do it for yourself...and then what? Sure you need to resolve your geist's issues before you can move on but your character's main motivation has been resolved<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm overthinking it since we don't see as much of sin eater society, it could be that finding yourself after this resolution is a big thing and the main reasons krews form in the first place. Okay i'm done... now what?... I know I'll be a spooky ghost person! It just seems that doing that would be like making changeling types based around a fetch. An important part of the character sure but not one that will last the entire chronicle nine times out of ten and not for every player. Hoping to see the next preview address this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eric Draven was a character specifically designed for a short-form chronicle, so his specific expression of the Vengeful Burden was straightforward and direct. In a longer-form game, the ST would encourage his player to create a more involved Burden. Basically, just like Aspirations can be short-term or long-term, so can Burdens, and we're going to give you advice on talking to your ST about how lengthy a process it is to fulfill yours--but we <i>do</i> expect that most PCs will fulfill their Burdens in a typical game, and that &quot;well, what do I do <i>now</i>?&quot; is very much a question that cuts to the core of the game's themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T09:36:48-07:00","id":1155094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1154848#post1154848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the antagonists- the Reapers seems to remind me a antagonist concept I've had for ages, even though I've pictured those antagonists as the emissaries of the Kerebros instead of the Deathloths/Chthonic Gods. I do like the more active role the Chthonic Gods take in the setting. I also how different they would end up from the Chthonians (I think they are not the same kind of entity, but right now I'm not sure).</div> </div> </div> </div>Cthonic Gods are the maybe-imaginary maybe-anthropmorphized-features-of-the-Underworld offscreen things that 1e called Deathlords. If they exist, they don't have mechanics.<br /> Reapers and Cthonians are both within the bounds of the Storytelling system, and the game's expansion of the ghost rules covers both of them. They aren't the same thing, which I can't explain until Travis tells you what a Reaper <i>is</i>. But a Cthonian is what it's always been - one of the rare, powerful, Never-born, native entities of the Underworld, that kills ghosts with a simple touch but (fortunately) doesn't seem to <i>notice</i> them, or have anything like a human perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T10:13:08-07:00","id":1155110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1155094#post1155094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cthonic Gods are the maybe-imaginary maybe-anthropmorphized-features-of-the-Underworld offscreen things that 1e called Deathlords. If they exist, they don't have mechanics.<br /> Reapers and Cthonians are both within the bounds of the Storytelling system, and the game's expansion of the ghost rules covers both of them. They aren't the same thing, which I can't explain until Travis tells you what a Reaper <i>is</i>. But a Cthonian is what it's always been - one of the rare, powerful, Never-born, native entities of the Underworld, that kills ghosts with a simple touch but (fortunately) doesn't seem to <i>notice</i> them, or have anything like a human perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do chtonians have any kind of special ability,something others can't do ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T10:45:04-07:00","id":1155130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1155110#post1155110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do chtonians have any kind of special ability,something others can't do ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> They're not ghosts. They use the ephemeral entity rules without being ghosts the same way Goetia, Angels, Abyssal entities and Supernal entities do, because the mechanical differences between them and ghosts can fit onto one page. They're much more at home in the Underworld than ghosts - even Kerberoi - are, but a cthonian in the living world is like a jellyfish in the Gobi Desert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T10:49:20-07:00","id":1155131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1155130#post1155130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> They're not ghosts. They use the ephemeral entity rules without being ghosts the same way Goetia, Angels, Abyssal entities and Supernal entities do, because the mechanical differences between them and ghosts can fit onto one page. They're much more at home in the Underworld than ghosts - even Kerberoi - are, but a cthonian in the living world is like a jellyfish in the Gobi Desert.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you Dave","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:19:09-07:00","id":1155138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1155130#post1155130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> They're not ghosts. They use the ephemeral entity rules without being ghosts the same way Goetia, Angels, Abyssal entities and Supernal entities do, because the mechanical differences between them and ghosts can fit onto one page. They're much more at home in the Underworld than ghosts - even Kerberoi - are, but a cthonian in the living world is like a jellyfish in the Gobi Desert.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent does that make them relatively weak(er) or lost/aimless if they somehow end up in the Living World? I always kind of wonder what level of threat a Cthonian would be if one accidentally ended up there or what their effect on the living would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:40:48-07:00","id":1155149,"title":"","content":"This first dev blog has really got me excited and curious for more information <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I remember a mention is previous forums of a supporting cast minor splat in the upcoming 2E appendices, somewhat analogous to the proximi and sleepwalkers of Mage the Awakening or Wolf-Blooded from Werewolf the Forsaken. Any chance there's been further word of that nature? or of the Y splat set up for Gesit 2e?? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:51:16-07:00","id":1155152,"title":"","content":"And on the Cthonian note. I wonder if the jellyfish analogy is a reference to the both the unsuitability of that creature type to the environment of the living world, and the toxicity of that type to souls, ghosts and echoes of the living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T12:44:56-07:00","id":1155169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1155152#post1155152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And on the Cthonian note. I wonder if the jellyfish analogy is a reference to the both the unsuitability of that creature type to the environment of the living world, and the toxicity of that type to souls, ghosts and echoes of the living.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even dead and dessicated jellyfish still sting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1155094#post1155094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cthonic Gods are the maybe-imaginary maybe-anthropmorphized-features-of-the-Underworld offscreen things that 1e called Deathlords. If they exist, they don't have mechanics. Reapers and Cthonians are both within the bounds of the Storytelling system, and the game's expansion of the ghost rules covers both of them. They aren't the same thing, which I can't explain until Travis tells you what a Reaper <i>is</i>. But a Cthonian is what it's always been - one of the rare, powerful, Never-born, native entities of the Underworld, that kills ghosts with a simple touch but (fortunately) doesn't seem to <i>notice</i> them, or have anything like a human perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Wait, Chthonians can kill ghosts with a touch? That's new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T18:13:25-07:00","id":1155238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div c