ttachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T14:08:27-08:00","id":1183698,"title":"","content":"Voted for Keys and Haunts, simply because I want to see how changed in the new system from the original one. Anyway, I must say that I do enjoy the new direction that Geist is having, and the fact it has now explained why the Sin Eaters do not have an &quot;appropriate culture&quot;- not to mention how the origin of &quot;Sin Eating&quot; was played in the blog. It all helps Geist feel much more like an appropriate monsters, instead of &quot;voodoo superheroes&quot;. Still, I feel like something is a bit missing for me- some spark of some kind, the whole &quot;second chances&quot; and &quot;carnival of life and death&quot; themes, which really click &quot;Geist&quot; to me. Of course, I'm not going to scream &quot;RUINED FOREVER&quot; because one blog post or anything like that, but I do hope that we would see that theme of celebrating life in death, and that the fact that you are dead does not mean your life are over yet.<br /> <br /> Also, after Geist would be out, I'm probably going to revise my ghul micro template, as it also use the whole &quot;dead people who just keep on walking&quot; motif.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I 