con__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1230539#post1230539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aokigahara would be neat if there is a Japan setting, but I can definitely understand not using it as a setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that the &quot;suicide forest?&quot; That would be a sensitive one, yes.<br /> <br /> Eastern Europe seems like a good place, as it was occupied by both Nazis and Soviet satellites.<br /> <br /> Mexico is just so much of a must, I'll eat a figurative hat if it's not in there.<br /> <br /> Given that the Underworld has become even more watery in aesthetic, somewhere that's watery in the living world seems like a neat idea. My first thought was Venice, but that's too close to Eastern Europe maybe. Jakarta or Manila?<br /> In the same vein, somewhere in the desert. Maybe somewhere associated with history and opulence, like Samarkand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T09:28:59-07:00","id":1230565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1230564#post1230564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that the &quot;suicide forest?&quot; That would be a sensitive one, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Aokigahara has already been used for <i>Demon</i>. It's in the Storyteller's Guide as a large-scale piece of Infrastructure that uses the willing deaths of the suicides to keep Mt. Fuji from erupting, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 06-27-2018, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T16:31:32-07:00","id":1230678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition?p=1230564#post1230564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that the &quot;suicide forest?&quot; That would be a sensitive one, yes.<br /> <br /> Eastern Europe seems like a good place, as it was occupied by both Nazis and Soviet satellites.<br /> <br /> Mexico is just so much of a must, I'll eat a figurative hat if it's not in there.<br /> <br /> Given that the Underworld has become even more watery in aesthetic, somewhere that's watery in the living world seems like a neat idea. My first thought was Venice, but that's too close to Eastern Europe maybe. Jakarta or Manila?<br /> In the same vein, somewhere in the desert. Maybe somewhere associated with history and opulence, like Samarkand.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, the imagery of a dry heat desert sludgingly opening to a vast and dark underworld set of rivers of the dead has a nice look in my mind. <br /> <br /> Especially since the Underworld seems almost parasitic. The &quot;Water-of-the-Below&quot; and the arid &quot;Dry-of-the-Above&quot; has a pretty cool dichotomy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T17:47:23-07:00","id":1230694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"q